==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Dogenstein]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*3 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*1 [[Angelic Gory]] spawns after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Johnnyleon]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Director Kurosawah]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
**1 [[Shachiko]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage introduces Shachiko, a [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] variant of [[Dolphina]] that acts almost exactly the same. Unfortunately for Shachiko, being both a Relic and a [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] enemy means [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:NX]] can stack both [[Insane Damage]] vs. Relic and [[Sage Slayer]] multipliers against it, resulting in Idi:NX being able to two-shot Shachiko.

Shachiko's debut in particular is incredibly straightforward: there's only one Shachiko, meaning once you lure Shachiko and nuke it with Idi you basically win. Bring units to deal with the multiple Angelic Gories like [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Master of Mind Soractes]] and something to speed up Kurosawah's cleanup like  [[Talents|Talented]] [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T]] and you should beat this stage easily.

==Trivia==
*Like most [[Forest Playground]] stages, Bamboocopter Launch's name is a reference to a toy. In this case, a [[wikipedia:Bamboo-copter|bamboo-copter]] is a toy helicopter rotor that flies up into the air when its shaft is rapidly spun and released. Another name for this toy is "bamboo dragonfly", which is part of the stage's Japanese name, Taketonbo-gun Kiji (竹とんぼ群生地, "Bamboo Dragonfly Colony").

